# Fault clearing and reclosing on a 132 kV line feeding a 33 kV substation
#
#   GRID (132 kV, sequence impedance) -- BRK (3 poles, open at current zero) -- LINE (50 km, pi)
#        -- T1 (132/33 kV, YNd1, saturating core) -- 33 kV load (30 MW, 10 Mvar)
#   Surge arresters at the line end; single-line-to-ground fault on phase a at the line end.
#
# Events
#   40 ms   fault phase a to ground at the line end
#   80 ms   breaker trip command: each pole opens at its own current zero
#   120 ms  fault arc extinguishes
#   165 ms  breaker recloses at a phase-a voltage zero: the line and transformer are re-energised (inrush)
#
# Elements used: V3 behind sequence impedance, SW with czero, PI3, XF3 with saturation, MOV, F.
#
# Generated by circuits/make_drawings.py; open it in the circuit editor (gui.bat) to see the drawing.
#
# EMTSim netlist: fault clearing and reclosing (drawn with the EMTSim circuit editor)
#
# Format: R/L/C from to value | V from to peak angle freq [R] | SW from to closed|open times... | F from to t_apply [t_clear]
# 12 nodes (4 three-phase nodes), 16 elements
# Three-phase drawing: node k of the drawing is netlist node 3k-2 (phase a), 3k-1 (b) and 3k (c)

.tran 0.00005 0.25

V3 1 2 3  107778 0 50  1 0.05 2 0.12   # GRID
SW 1 4  closed 0.08 0.165 czero   # BRK.a
SW 2 5  closed 0.08 0.165 czero   # BRK.b
SW 3 6  closed 0.08 0.165 czero   # BRK.c
PI3 4 5 6 7 8 9  2.5 0.065 4.5e-7 7.5 0.2 3e-7   # LINE
MOV 7 0  172000 1000 26   # ARR.a
MOV 8 0  172000 1000 26   # ARR.b
MOV 9 0  172000 1000 26   # ARR.c
F 7 0  0.04 0.12   # FAULT.a
XF3 7 8 9 10 11 12  YNd1 60000000 132000 33000 50 0.12 0.005 im=0.5 knee=1.15 lsat=0.3   # T1
R 10 0  36.3   # LOAD_R.a
R 11 0  36.3   # LOAD_R.b
R 12 0  36.3   # LOAD_R.c
L 10 0  0.347   # LOAD_L.a
L 11 0  0.347   # LOAD_L.b
L 12 0  0.347   # LOAD_L.c

